issue_context.body:
**Is your enhancement proposal related to a problem? Please describe.**
We have some module to handle service discovery. This module does the whole discovery, caches all the outputs and when it finishes, it provides easy interface for the application. For a reference you can see it here (https://github.com/NordicPlayground/fw-nrfconnect-nrf/blob/master/subsys/bluetooth/gatt_dm.c).

Now we wish to add CEP (GATT Characteristic Extended Properties) support directly into it.
To get all the CEP attributes values I wish to use **Read By Type Request**. I could use ``bt_gatt_read`` with ``params::handle_count`` set to 0, and I should get what I wish, but it would force me to add ``bt_gatt_read_params`` structure data into my instance. But all the data I really need is still there in my ``bt_gatt_discovery_params`` instance. To limit memory usage and data copying I wish to have a possibility to read CEP using my ``bt_gatt_discovery_params``.

**Describe the solution you'd like**
__Implement the required functionality into discovery function.__
We have all the data which we need: uuid is here, start and end handle is also here. We just need additional functionality like BT_GATT_DISCOVER_READ.

**Describe alternatives you've considered**
We can align discovery and read data, it seems quite similar, but only include data inside discovery seems to break the interoperability:

__Align read and discover structures layout.__
Then we do not need anything more, and probably we do not need to modify the code.
Just add a possibility to create discovery and read structures union with all the critical data in place.

Lets look how it looks now:
```
struct bt_gatt_read_params {
	struct bt_att_req _req;
	bt_gatt_read_func_t func;
	size_t handle_count;
	union {
		struct {
			u16_t handle;
			u16_t offset;
		} single;
		u16_t *handles;
		struct {
			u16_t start_handle;
			u16_t end_handle;
			struct bt_uuid *uuid;
		} by_uuid;
	};
};
```

```
struct bt_gatt_discover_params {
	struct bt_att_req _req;
	/** Discover UUID type */
	struct bt_uuid *uuid;
	/** Discover attribute callback */
	bt_gatt_discover_func_t func;
	union {
		struct {
			/** Include service attribute declaration handle */
			u16_t attr_handle;
			/** Included service start handle */
			u16_t start_handle;
			/** Included service end handle */
			u16_t end_handle;
		} _included;
		/** Discover start handle */
		u16_t start_handle;
	};
	/** Discover end handle */
	u16_t end_handle;
	/** Discover type */
	u8_t type;
};
```
If we can move somehow the _included at the end, rest of the fields seems to be easily organized to match the others: uuid needs to be moved, and type from discovery would be placed together with handle_count from read.

But still - the _included inside discovery structure messes it a lot - not sure if it may be easy done.

**Additional context**
NC

comments:
@Vudentz Are you saying then that we should have a way to read CEP using `bt_gatt_discovery_params` or not?

The size optimization of the params is not really a blocker for this feature request. Do you suggest to do it in that order anyway, and do you intend to both yourself?

Leaving caching of the discovered attributes and values up to the application is perfectly fine. Don't need to have that in the host, the use-case decides what needs to be stored.
